From e18ceed8ff8546c1598c845eefc53f2db905c437 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:59:14 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Serve public pages from cache and refresh them on Sanity
 changes

The [locale] layout forced every page to render on every request
(force-dynamic, revalidate 0), so each visit re-ran the server render and
the Sanity queries. Pages are now pre-rendered per locale (blog/project/
category detail pages on first visit) and refreshed by SanityLive, a new
signed Sanity webhook (/api/revalidate) and a one-hour fallback.

Also caches the list/search JSON routes on the CDN for a minute (never in
draft mode), rebuilds the sitemap at most hourly, and lowers Sentry trace
and replay sampling in production, since every event goes through the
/monitoring tunnel as a function call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Au13BHPjUgRvpqWWWW3dF
